xlint react/purity) and gets its co-located test.","tree":{"sha":"6c84aa927f9fc83122db84bfd9ee15d6194785e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/trees/6c84aa927f9fc83122db84bfd9ee15d6194785e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/commits/bad0820f26d202bbdda7a996f02d215da9b72d6c","verification":{"payload":"tree 6c84aa927f9fc83122db84bfd9ee15d6194785e4\nparent f895803526da84ed0c6f23c76871417679c2d7a7\nauthor Vadym Kononenko <70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com> 1791442057 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791442057 +0300\n\nchore(deps): newest compatible versions; holds and the cooldown bypass recorded (#95)\n\nPackages younger than the 3-day cooldown were taken on purpose; DECISIONS lists each\nwith its publish date and provenance. Holds stay only for measured incompatibilities:\nmsw 3 (vitest''s mocker peers msw 2 and imports a path msw 3 removed), TypeScript 7\n(typescript-eslint peer), vitest 5 (Stryker runs zero tests per mutant), @types/node 26.\ntypescript-eslint 8.71 false-fires no-unsafe-enum-assignment on createSelectors\n(upstream #12966): off for that one file until the fix ships.\nDead overrides removed; js-yaml security floors keyed by major; the MSW worker is\nregenerated for the installed msw. Vite config imports carry .ts extensions and use\nimport.meta.dirname, so the native config loader no longer warns. The footer reads the\nyear once at module load (oxlint react/purity) and gets its co-located test.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxzyJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA54EQAGQ/uFzGo2mk2UEfDrcQD3el\npx18TjHExThZhDi1qh6/DwjRBmWqfsPYuqWMUUD2vrkMdnU/z7Sd/cixyXF2DFGF\nmRarpxLbLuYjYU0JTYxOhWC8GFPtqlDnQDx+TxP2EBJyi12jwbPiYg4ibKT3rit+\nmD76i/O4pUWYf3R4dgAG7inr+a1X29420bgMc1xRp6z5rFPhJCAwPQG+WvI7vVwh\nPloFmZf/+JU87U9ydJnf8ASRxxs9jBhjN2GR4bkGHQBPSEJUcaWYEYdEml1L9ACu\nBKasJjVg5C28gmPiSewjPsGuoT+256I7tDZrfwoOwVfjsbvaK9RBsu4pRY2aAjSP\nh6wCrH9iHvfSzw8TaQDFPwoSXs+GW8uT