rs/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95/template-1/commit/f5a873169835f08a6a9606cf7723562145b599ff","node_id":"C_kwDOQT0KedoAKGY1YTg3MzE2OTgzNWYwOGE2YTk2MDZjZjc3MjM1NjIxNDViNTk5ZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95/template-1/commit/ced02393dae5c25ec8e966a4a63e1d27405780de","sha":"ced02393dae5c25ec8e966a4a63e1d27405780de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/ced02393dae5c25ec8e966a4a63e1d27405780de"}],"sha":"f5a873169835f08a6a9606cf7723562145b599ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/f5a873169835f08a6a9606cf7723562145b599ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70842045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95","id":70842045,"login":"Vadymk95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQyMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/ced02393dae5c25ec8e966a4a63e1d27405780de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:27:35Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T19:27:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gate): the push budget calibrates to the machine it runs on, not to mine (#69)\n\n* fix(gate): the push budget calibrates to the machine it runs on, not to mine\n\nA committed number of seconds describes ONE machine and nothing in the file said which. In\na template that is the worst possible place for it: every fork inherited a ceiling it might\nbe unable to meet, read red from its third push onward, and had two remedies - raise the\nnumber or stop looking. The spread is not small. The same two suites measured 5.6x and\n10.5x slower on a two-core runner than on the workstation that set these numbers.\n\nSo there are no seconds in git any more. `gate-tiers.json` holds a ratio and a sample size,\nwhich mean the same thing everywhere. The gate calibrates a baseline from its OWN first\nruns, per phase, into the gitignored `.gate-budget.json` beside the tracer log it already\nwrites, and reports drift past that ratio.\n\nThe baseline ratchets DOWN by itself, the shape a lint or type baseline already uses: a gate\nthat gets genuinely faster lowers the bar it will be held to next time, with no edit and no\ndecision. It rises only when someone deletes the file, which is the honest way to say this\nis the new normal.\n\nTwo of these four were reading RED against their old hardcoded numbers while their recent\nruns were comfortably inside. That is the failure this replaces, not a coincidence.\n\n`budgetReport` stays pure - it reads no file and writes none, the caller does the I/O - so\nevery branch is tested without a filesystem, including the one that matters most: the same\ngate on hardware three times slower reports the same verdict.\n\n* fix(gate): read the baseline without checking first, which was a file-system race\n\nCodeQL caught it on the pull request that introduced it, at high severity\n(js/file-system-race): `existsSync` then `readFileSync` on a path this function also WRITES\nis a check-then-use, and the file may change in between.\n\nRead and catch instead. That also folds in the case the check never handled - a file left\nhalf-written by an interrupted run - and both mean the same thing here, which is that this\nmachine has no baseline yet. Verified: a corrupt .gate-budget.json now recalibrates instead\nof throwing and taking docs:check down with it.\n\nWorth recording why this was found at all: it is the first pull request these templates have\nopened. Every previous change went straight to master, where the pull-request checks never\nrun - so CodeQL''s PR analysis had never once looked at this code.\n\n* docs(agents): say what a fork does NOT inherit, because settings do not travel\n\nThe pull-request section added earlier today tells the reader that master carries a ruleset\nrequiring the `validate` check. True here, false in every fork: rulesets, branch protection,\nrequired checks, Actions permissions, secret scanning and CodeQL are repository SETTINGS,\nand a fork is a new repository that starts with none of them. Only files travel.\n\nSo a fork arrives with the entire gate and none of the enforcement, and nothing on screen\nsays so. The hooks run, CI runs on pull requests, and a push straight to the default branch\nis stopped by nothing at all.\n\nREADME now lists what is not inherited and the cheapest order to switch it on: enable\nActions, open one pull request so the checks register their names, then add a ruleset\nrequiring `validate`. That last step is what turns the README from description into\nenforcement.\n\nAlso named there because it is the easiest thing to miss: `.npmrc` disables lifecycle\nscripts on purpose, so `npm install` alone leaves a fork with no git hooks.","tree":{"sha":"f06a9597b6f17438da58c21de2247d1354ace522","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/trees/f06a9597b6f17438da58c21de2247d1354ace522"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/commits/ced02393dae5c25ec8e966a4a63e1d27405780de","verification":{"payload":"tree f06a9597b6f17438da58c21de2247d1354ace522\nparent 7f0673cecf6d05d7c3ed410e19986b800a06dd65\nauthor Vadym Kononenko <70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com> 1789327655 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789327655 +0300\n\nfix(gate): the push budget calibrates to the machine it runs on, not to mine (#69)\n\n* fix(gate): the push budget calibrates to the machine it runs on, not to mine\n\nA committed number of seconds describes ONE machine and nothing in the file said which. In\na template that is the worst possible place for it: every fork inherited a ceiling it might\nbe unable to meet, read red from its third push onward, and had two remedies - raise the\nnumber or stop looking. The spread is not small. The same two suites measured 5.6x and\n10.5x slower on a two-core runner than on the workstation that set these numbers.\n\nSo there are no seconds in git any more. `gate-tiers.json` holds a ratio and a sample size,\nwhich mean the same thing everywhere. The gate calibrates a baseline from its OWN first\nruns, per phase, into the gitignored `.gate-budget.json` beside the tracer log it already\nwrites, and reports drift past that ratio.\n\nThe baseline ratchets DOWN by itself, the shape a lint or type baseline already uses: a gate\nthat gets genuinely faster lowers the bar it will be held to next time, with no edit and no\ndecision. It rises only when someone deletes the file, which is the honest way to say this\nis the new normal.\n\nTwo of these four were reading RED against their old hardcoded numbers while their recent\nruns were comfortably inside. That is the failure this replaces, not a coincidence.\n\n`budgetReport` stays pure - it reads no file and writes none, the caller does the I/O - so\nevery branch is tested without a filesystem, including the one that matters most: the same\ngate on hardware three times slower reports the same verdict.\n\n* fix(gate): read the baseline without checking first, which was a file-system race\n\nCodeQL caught it on the pull request that introduced it, at high severity\n(js/file-system-race): `existsSync` then `readFileSync` on a path this function also WRITES\nis a check-then-use, and the file may change in between.\n\nRead and catch instead. That also folds in the case the check never handled - a file left\nhalf-written by an interrupted run - and both mean the same thing here, which is that this\nmachine has no baseline yet. Verified: a corrupt .gate-budget.json now recalibrates instead\nof throwing and taking docs:check down with it.\n\nWorth recording why this was found at all: it is the first pull request these templates have\nopened. Every previous change went straight to master, where the pull-request checks never\nrun - so CodeQL''s PR analysis had never once looked at this code.\n\n* docs(agents): say what a fork does NOT inherit, because settings do not travel\n\nThe pull-request section added earlier today tells the reader that master carries a ruleset\nrequiring the `validate` check. True here, false in every fork: rulesets, branch protection,\nrequired checks, Actions permissions, secret scanning and CodeQL are repository SETTINGS,\nand a fork is a new repository that starts with none of them. Only files travel.\n\nSo a fork arrives with the entire gate and none of the enforcement, and nothing on screen\nsays so. The hooks run, CI runs on pull requests, and a push straight to the default branch\nis stopped by nothing at all.\n\nREADME now lists what is not inherited and the cheapest order to switch it on: enable\nActions, open one pull request so the checks register their names, then add a ruleset\nrequiring `validate`. That last step is what turns the README from description into\nenforcement.\n\nAlso named there because it is the easiest thing to miss: `.npmrc` disables lifecycle\nscripts on purpose, so `npm install` alone leaves a fork with no git hooks.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpvknCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc/sQAIRD/u3k//uUdhqgbdUcaS8a\nNOBLSkxnPR/8v/xhinQ4E9Er+Az7j6SgHfjz09eT2IJhOcxZRl3Pbgxq4ZrB525z\n7UGPAsAufQa1n6O6+0upnvkh37Ovql3zL/qFDfkktsg7nZ8z3OE1VgXcC7Qy9095\nRv5q94hMzDBMIvQnyjTq5P0fnXYO3POwbB5p+M2L7MEb8+MgTHEhPmXYiygok6Po\nxR3TMtk+eevQ4s51wkNOECClzv9s6gGwes2+IDPs/BrPDBD8AKlmX2scR6ZgnV9j\nUbewD/AIm4RUGW+6JaB+MnJxN+lxROAGsjYk4cetF99UC35VKnUHv/HZJC8PQeuw\ndE1J4EA1KdbqPj2up+VirtnPzP/wdBeBtOP2O/E4Bb/6v6pcJeqG5JkZ1mn9UVqo\ncUeUZBD7q6X67Xi14mnAc77clQPFMNMMndiX+PeIm3H1OYOiin/Q12d37POqD99a\n20U+7D0d7mp7DI547D3namyA5b3wu66XS0uQW7IiFc2Ix43MoQsiyw+u1vebXWiB\nAEfCRA8uk0qSegEuVixg7WORcCqRMt0HwbPn1Sae1/ChX7LeTn0IqhdhFXZDMciv\nxQ/QkSBrkWJOsh/nFB9cVmGuw1HT7yNHT+9MGPJsQdkAFQKlkgcYfHFti9LDs4F9\nW5icpE+qqgfAXkrj4R+p\n=DYrH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-13T19:27:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95/template-1/commit/ced02393dae5c25ec8e966a4a63e1d27405780de","node_id":"C_kwDOQT0KedoAKGNlZDAyMzkzZGFlNWMyNWVjOGU5NjZhNGE2M2UxZDI3NDA1NzgwZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95/template-1/commit/7f0673cecf6d05d7c3ed410e19986b800a06dd65","sha":"7f0673cecf6d05d7c3ed410e19986b800a06dd65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/7f0673cecf6d05d7c3ed410e19986b800a06dd65"}],"sha":"ced02393dae5c25ec8e966a4a63e1d27405780de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/ced02393dae5c25ec8e966a4a63e1d27405780de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70842045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95","id":70842045,"login":"Vadymk95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQyMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/7f0673cecf6d05d7c3ed410e19986b800a06dd65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T17:34:09Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T17:34:09Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"message":"fix(gate): give the push budget a recency window so it can recover\n\nA budget with no window cannot come back from a bad day. Measured in a sibling repository on\n2026-09-13, in one afternoon and in order: p90 350.8s over 33 runs, 359.3s over 34, 382.0s\nover 35 - while the suite it measures got 192s of cumulative browser time FASTER in the same\nwindow. The tail that moved it was two runs taken on a workstation running four other gates.\n\nThe budget then reads red on a healthy suite, and the tempting fix is to raise it, which is\nexactly what a budget exists to prevent. p90 now comes from the last 20 successful runs in\nthe phase and the message says \"the last 20 of 35\" so the window is visible in the output\nrather than implied. Twenty is long enough that one slow run does not swing it and short\nenough that a fixed suite shows up.\n\nNo window set keeps the old behaviour, so the reading is unchanged wherever the data block\ndoes not carry one.","tree":{"sha":"be5143a031b50dab5e237ba739f0b2625fd1c5ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/trees/be5143a031b50dab5e237ba739f0b2625fd1c5ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/commits/7f0673cecf6d05d7c3ed410e19986b800a06dd65","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70842045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95","id":70842045,"login":"Vadymk95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQyMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95/template-1/commit/7f0673cecf6d05d7c3ed410e19986b800a06dd65","node_id":"C_kwDOQT0KedoAKDdmMDY3M2NlY2Y2ZDA1ZDdjM2VkNDEwZTE5OTg2YjgwMGEwNmRkNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95/template-1/commit/151eaaa7802f9b608767cd889fb221b3853490a5","sha":"151eaaa7802f9b608767cd889fb221b3853490a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/151eaaa7802f9b608767cd889fb221b3853490a5"}],"sha":"7f0673cecf6d05d7c3ed410e19986b800a06dd65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/7f0673cecf6d05d7c3ed410e19986b800a06dd65"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70842045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95","id":70842045,"login":"Vadymk95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQyMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/151eaaa7802f9b608767cd889fb221b3853490a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:40:11Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:40:11Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"message":"fix(gate): let release-please own the changelog format instead of the checker\n\nThe first push after the 3.2.0 release was rejected by the gate''s own format:check, on a\nfile nobody edited. release-please writes CHANGELOG.md in its own markdown dialect - `*`\nbullets and no blank line after the heading - and Prettier prefers `-`, so every release\nnow hands the next pusher a red gate.\n\nReformatting the file would be undone by the next release, so the generator keeps its\noutput and the checker stops reading it. All four templates were in the same state; this is\na regression of the release mechanism that landed the same day, caught the first time\nanyone tried to push after a release.","tree":{"sha":"eb0d196ab4d13ca22235b9b706bf08ed3ad80355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/trees/eb0d196ab4d13ca22235b9b706bf08ed3ad80355"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/commits/151eaaa7802f9b608767cd889fb221b3853490a5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70842045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95","id":70842045,"login":"Vadymk95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQyMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95/template-1/commit/151eaaa7802f9b608767cd889fb221b3853490a5","node_id":"C_kwDOQT0KedoAKDE1MWVhYWE3ODAyZjliNjA4NzY3Y2Q4ODlmYjIyMWIzODUzNDkwYTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95/template-1/commit/bcc58d8a5628cbd4348d6841ca528647b823739d","sha":"bcc58d8a5628cbd4348d6841ca528647b823739d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/bcc58d8a5628cbd4348d6841ca528647b823739d"}],"sha":"151eaaa7802f9b608767cd889fb221b3853490a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/151eaaa7802f9b608767cd889fb221b3853490a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70842045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vadymk95","id":70842045,"login":"Vadymk95","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQyMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/bcc58d8a5628cbd4348d6841ca528647b823739d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:37:59Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:38:53Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"message":"fix(gate): make eslint blind to an agent worktree inside the repository\n\nAn agent worktree created under the repository root is a full second checkout, and every\nentry in globalIgnores is root-anchored, so its copies walk straight past all of them.\n\nMeasured with a probe file at .claude/worktrees/probe on 2026-09-13: eslint linted 150\nfiles with the probe present and 149 without this line, counting the copy as ours.\n\nVitest is immune here and that is by construction rather than by luck - its `include` is an\nexplicit whitelist of root-anchored globs (src, vite-plugins, scripts, e2e/support), so a\npath outside them is never collected; the probe confirmed it at 0. tsc is immune because\nits globs skip dot-directories, and oxlint because it honours .gitignore, which already\ncovers .claude.\n\nSame class as the `.stryker-tmp` entry two lines up. The rule stays what it was - agent\nworktrees belong OUTSIDE the repository - and this line is what makes the gate independent\nof anyone remembering it. Found in a sibling repository the same day, where the equivalent\ngap let vitest run another checkout''s tests and turn the gate red.","tree":{"sha":"46324f3145b5fe6e4a64ba31eef3c0fb319d4900","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/trees/46324f3145b5fe6e4a64ba31eef3c0fb319d4900"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/commits/bcc58d8a5628cbd4348d6841ca528647b823739d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70842045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/gists{/gist_id}