admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/d7b0e69737af445a1a63b6c691ec15d31dd60640/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T15:36:54Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T15:36:54Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"message":"docs(gate): delete the leftover copies - pointers only, and no hand-run of the full chain\n\nSecond sweep after the law moved into one file. Removed: the transitional \"until\n2026-08-30 this said X\" clauses (our repo history, useless to a fork - the record\nlives in the vault note); a duplicate command block that survived below the\nrewritten one; every passage still ORDERING a hand-run of verify / verify:full,\nwhich contradicted the law it sat next to; and the last stale rung list that\nstill said the gate runs once before hand-over.\n\nRewritten rather than deleted where the advice was right but named the wrong\ncommand: content-variance and geometry work is the MEASURE moment, not the full\nchain, and a single spec goes through e2e:one so the tracer sees the most\nexpensive stage instead of being stepped around. The exit-code-without-a-pipe\nlesson now demonstrates on verify:iter - the same discipline on a command the\nreader may actually run. What stays everywhere is a one-line pointer: a file that\ndiscusses verification and says nothing about the moment is how an agent\nre-derives \"run everything\".","tree":{"sha":"eb232d0d9d1be88042523ca3751fbee6294cfece","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/trees/eb232d0d9d1be88042523ca3751fbee6294cfece"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/templa