api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/commits/8a394b5443250c657c533899ee6ce7f682613f77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T13:42:26Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T13:42:26Z","email":"70842045+Vadymk95@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vadym Kononenko"},"message":"docs: record the content-variance gate and the cross-engine findings\n\nWhat the gate is, why the fixture is dev-only and what that costs, why counts are\nderived, and the two rules that were earned: the range of widths a guard covers is\npart of its specification, and a wrap class with no red-to-green proof gets deleted\nrather than kept for safety.\n\nThe verification integrity section gains the falsification question and the three\nshapes that pass while measuring nothing here: a page still hidden by the i18n\nboot gate, a testMatch that selects no tests, and a coverage run that drops a file\nit could not parse.\n\nAlso records what cross-engine running actually found - Firefox reports\nclientWidth 0 for an inline label per CSSOM where Chromium reports a box - and one\nknown deviation left unfixed on purpose, with the reason.","tree":{"sha":"1023d33f22b71da8ea23bc8387089bd216e8751b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/trees/1023d33f22b71da8ea23bc8387089bd216e8751b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vadymk95/template-1/git/commits/8a394b5443250c657c533899ee6ce7f682613f77","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70842045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vadymk95/followers","following_url":"https: