k control (budget, expenses,\nmeetings, meeting detail, payment pot, Tricount, audience) now get one\nunder the redesign flag: a shell inset row, or the screen''s own toolbar\nwhen it pushes a detail so the system back button takes its place.\n\nHub actions route through pure, rollout-aware rules: without the\ninvitation rollout, participants and draft dates open the legacy\nparticipant screen, the recap opens poll results and the info menu item\nis hidden. Tile locks now mirror the destination guards so no open tile\nleads to an access-denied screen.\n\nRefs Swarm DAO #47 (layer 4).","tree":{"sha":"7c3e65ec85b505c0846f4a5cc0ac045e1daca504","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guyghost/wakeve/git/trees/7c3e65ec85b505c0846f4a5cc0ac045e1daca504"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guyghost/wakeve/git/commits/8f823550c62821dc9c294e3fdd98796f14e17496","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c3e65ec85b505c0846f4a5cc0ac045e1daca504\nparent 42b5bf2b6e5a55365c7e3db716f7c7dfa0c33767\nauthor Guy MANDINA <guyghost@gmail.com> 1790766798 +0200\ncommitter Guy MANDINA <guyghost@gmail.com> 1790766798 +0200\n\nfix(ios): remove dead ends around the event hub\n\nScreens reached from the hub without a back control (budget, expenses,\nmeetings, meeting detail, payment pot, Tricount, audience) now get one\nunder the redesign flag: a shell inset row, or the screen''s own toolbar\nwhen it pushes a detail so the system back button takes its place.\n\nHub actions route through pure, rollout-aware rules: without the\ninvitation rollout, participants and draft dates open the legacy\nparticipant screen, the recap opens poll results and the info menu item\nis hidden. Tile locks now mirror the destination guards so no open tile\nleads to an access-denied screen.\n\nRefs Swarm DAO #47 (layer 4).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQJPBAABCAA5FiEETEqlVEeZNKtOtBe951dUiAa843QFAmq87s8bFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMCwzAAoJEOdXVIgGvON0euIQAKagOL7FOTF6Z3LdhiLX\ny9SbfDZTB/gexm